{"text": "William Perry Pendle\nPost Office Box| oe\n\ncon\nPresident 1989-2018\nMountain States Legal Foundation\n\nChief executive, sole fundraiser, and spokesman for nationally known, nonprofit,\npublic-interest law firm that provides pro bono representation in precedent-setting legal\nand constitutional cases. Took organization from the edge of bankruptcy to $2.7 million\na year firm, with a $10 million endowment and its own national headquarters. Argued\nand won landmark cases before the Supreme Court of the United States and federal courts\nof appeals. Appear often on national television and radio shows. Author of five books,\nincluding Sagebrush Rebel: Reagan's Battle with Environmental Extremists and Why It\nMatters Today (Regnery, 2013), the definitive book on Reagan and the American West.\nPartner - Comiskey & Hunt; Washington, D.C. 1985 - 1989\n\nEnvironmental and natural resources attomey.\n\nLegal Assistant ~ Secretary of the Navy 1984 - 1985\nLegal researcher and writer for the United States Secretary of the Navy.\n\nDeputy Assistant Secretary ~ U.S. Department of the Interior 1981 - 1984\nManaged four federal agencies; authored two presidential proclamations.\n\nAttorney \u2014 United States House of Representatives 1978 - 1981\nEnvironmental and natural resources attorney for a House subcommittee.\n\nLegislative Assistant \u2014 United States Senate 1976 - 1978\n\nEnvironmental and natural resources attomey to a United States Senator.\nAdmitted to the practice of law: Colorado, Virginia, Wyoming, and Washington, D.C\n\nAuthor: Summary Judgment (MSLF, 2015)\nSagebrush Rebel (Regnery, 2013)\nWarriors for the West (Regnery, 2006)\nWar on the West (Regnery, 1995)\nIt Takes a Hero (Free Enterprise Press, 1994)\nNumerous law review articles, opinion-editorials, and syndicated columns\n\nMilitary: U.S. Marine Corps, Captain, Naval Flight Officer, 1969-1973.\nDegrees: B.A., Public Afiairs, George Washington University, 1967\n\nM.A., Public Affairs, George Washington University, 1968\nJ.D., University of Wyoming College of Law, 1976.",
